  "releaseNotes": "- [ThunderPropagator.BuildingBlocks#48] [Design] FeederMessage is both domain object and serialization DTO — introduce FeederMessageEnvelope / FeederMessagePayload separation   - FeederMessageEnvelope.cs (new) — concrete POCO with CorrelationId, HashKey, CastType, IsDeleted as real CLR auto-properties. Infrastructure code can now accept FeederMessageEnvelope directly to   reduce coupling to concrete message types.   - FeederMessagePayload.cs (new) — sealed dictionary wrapper (Dictionary<string, object?>) implementing both IDictionary<string, object?> and IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object?>. Exposes internal   helpers (SetValue, GetValue<T>, GetValueOrNull<T>, GetValueOrDefault<T>, Clear, ToDictionary) for FeederMessage to call. Remove/Clear via the interfaces throw NotSupportedException (semantically   correct vs the previous NotImplementedException).   - FeederMessage.cs (modified) — replaced the flat _dictionary with two backing stores:     - _envelope (FeederMessageEnvelope) for protocol fields; CastType, IsDeleted, CorrelationId, HashKey now delegate to it     - _payload (FeederMessagePayload) for user-defined fields; all SetValue/GetValue helpers and IDictionary members delegate to it     - Envelope and Payload public properties (both [IgnoreMember] for Phase 1 serialization compatibility) give infrastructure code direct access to each section     - Constructor is now block-bodied (per convention)\\n- [ThunderPropagator.BuildingBlocks#48] [Design] FeederMessage is both domain object and serialization DTO — introduce FeederMessageEnvelope / FeederMessagePayload separation   docs/RFC/RFC-48-FeederMessage-Envelope-Payload-Split.md — a full design RFC covering:",
